      "round_summary": "Repair round 1/3. Targeted all 3 failing properties (L6_count_is_one, count_never_exceeds_two, non_waiting_thread_completes_cycle). Error: dut_bug — the L2 handler unconditionally increments count, allowing count to overshoot to 3 when both threads reach L2 simultaneously due to unconstrained io_select scheduling. Fix 1 (L2, line 68): guard count increment with `when(count < 2.U)` to prevent overshoot. Fix 2 (L3, line 74): widen release condition from `count === 2.U` to `count >= 2.U || count === 0.U` so that a thread arriving at L3 after the other thread has already performed the release (resetting count to 0) still goes to L4 instead of getting stuck at L6. All 3 assertion labels preserved unchanged; no homologous assertions found — the two fixes are in distinct state handlers (L2, L3) serving complementary roles in the same causal path.",
